---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import data from '../data/bench.json';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="Rundale Bench — Methodology">
  <h2>Methodology</h2>

  <h3>Judge</h3>
  <p>
    Dialogue is scored by <strong>{data.judge_model}</strong> subagents launched
    from inside Claude Code. The judge config (<code>judge_sonnet_v1</code>) pins
    a <code>rubric_sha256</code>; any rubric edit without a matching hash bump
    aborts the run, so scores never drift silently.
  </p>

  <h3>Rubric — 5 axes (1–5)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Character</strong> — reads as an 1820 rural Irish midwife?</li>
    <li><strong>Authenticity</strong> — period vocabulary, no modern terms?</li>
    <li><strong>Language</strong> — English (en-IE) + optional Irish (ga-IE); no non-Latin script.</li>
    <li><strong>Responsiveness</strong> — actually addresses the prompt?</li>
    <li><strong>Craft</strong> — concise, evocative, 2–4 sentences.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Tier funnel</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>screen</strong> — ~5 prompts, every candidate.</li>
    <li><strong>contender</strong> — ~25 prompts; promoted at overall ≥ 3.5 and every axis &gt; 2.0.</li>
    <li><strong>finalist</strong> — full dev slice; promoted at overall ≥ 4.0 and every axis &gt; 3.0.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Quality vs perf</h3>
  <p>
    Quality is judged once per model on its cheapest provider. Latency, price,
    and throughput are measured separately for every provider serving the model
    — see the <a href={`${base}/perf`}>perf matrix</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Reproducibility</h3>
  <p>
    Each judgment is content-addressed by
    <code>sha256(prompt_id ‖ response_sha256 ‖ rubric_sha256 ‖ judge_model)</code>
    and committed under <code>docs/proofs/rundale-bench/judgments/</code>.
    Changing the rubric or judge re-judges everything; adding a model judges
    only that model.
  </p>
</Base>
